    "text": "how preportal works: a static site that feels dynamic how can a serverless blog feel dynamic? a walk through the preportal file layout, the publishing flow and how javascript builds the pages. preportal hosts no server: every page is plain html, css and javascript. content still behaves dynamically, because each post is a small javascript file inside the p/ folder and the pages read those files in the browser and build themselves instantly. folder layout p/ — posts ( p/slug.js ) users/ — authors ( users/user.js ) category/ — categories ( category/slug.js ) lang/ — language packs ( en.json , tr.json , ru.json ) data/ — index files: they declare which files to load index files keep the browser from guessing: it loads only the files that actually exist. publishing flow write the post in the publishing studio (ckeditor 5). on the “publish tool” tab, download the generated p/slug.js file. add the file to the repository and add the slug to data/posts.js . run node tools/build-index.js so search and crawlers see the new post. commit & push — github pages publishes within seconds. comments every post has its own disqus thread, identified by the post slug, so the conversation stays with the article even if the site moves. languages every interface string lives in a json language pack under lang/ . the globe button in the header switches between english, turkish and russian, and the choice is remembered in the browser. preportal github-pages javascript guide statik blog nasil kurulur g"
